out={'edition':'2.8','status':'conditional_planning_budget_not_procurement_or_total_company_cost','gbp_per_usd_assumption_not_live_fx':fx,'monthly_provider_anchors_gbp':monthly_gbp,'monthly_reserves_gbp_not_quotes':reserves,'monthly_before_cushion':base,'unallocated_tax_fx_usage_cushion_20pct':cushion,'monthly_operating_envelope':runrate,'upfront_items_gbp':oneoff,'upfront_total':upfront,'three_month_runway_excluding_build_pay':upfront+3*runrate,'six_month_runway_excluding_build_pay':upfront+6*runrate,'illustrative_monthly_engineering_allowance':engineering,'six_month_runway_with_engineering_allowance':upfront+6*(runrate+engineering),'not_priced':['initial_product_build_design_engineering','founder_pay_and_tax','company_specific_registration_insurance_legal_outliers','customer_acquisition_and_paid_ads','merchant_message_usage_beyond_minimums','large_map_traffic_or_native_update_overages','actual_store_billing_commissions_for_unsupported_digital_types','hardware_inventory_fulfilment_returns','support_load_beyond_current_capacity'],'scope':'both mobile app projects plus public web Studio Console API; all four software packages intended at launch'}
assert abs(base-191.288)<1e-8
(R/'launch-budget-results.json').write_text(json.dumps(out,indent=2)+'\n')
packages=json.loads((R/'proposed-packages.json').read_text())
f=lambda x:f'£{x:,.2f}'
lines=['# Taplo · Launch budget and package readout','', 'Working edition 2.8 · 3 November 2026. Conditional rough budget, not a quote or the full cost to build/operate Taplo. All four packages are intended at launch. No database/provider/store account has been opened or purchased by this blueprint work. Source facts are in the database/provider/store chapters; reserve figures are original planning assumptions.','', 'See LEAN-LAUNCH-SPENDING-AND-SECURITY.md: supplier anchors total £121.29/month; the £229.55 funded envelope includes reserves/cushion. The upfront table below is an optional review/device-funded scenario, not a minimum launch bill. Use existing suitable phones; digital Wallet QR testing needs no purchased NFC hardware. External review scope/cost is quoted separately from continuous internal work.','', '## The database decision, without salesmanship','', 'Neither Neon nor Supabase is configured, per founder clarification. Keep Neon Postgres as the current working greenfield selection because the proposed server-owned engine and recovery/branch economics fit it. Current Supabase is a valid integrated alternative; current Neon also has broader backend services. Neon is not objectively always cheaper/better and no migration saving is assumed. Comparable real capacity and engineering/operations effort still need measurement. A conditional “sign us up if better” is not treated as a completed account opening or a reason to purchase before selecting actual entity/account configuration.','', '## Monthly platform envelope at very early usage','', '| Provider anchor / explicit assumption | GBP/month |','| --- | ---: |']
for k,v in monthly_gbp.items():lines.append(f'| {k.replace("_"," ")} | {f(v)} |')
for k,v in reserves.items():lines.append(f'| {k.replace("_"," ")} — budget, not a quotation | {f(v)} |')
lines += [f'| Subtotal | {f(base)} |',f'| Unallocated 20% tax/FX/usage cushion | {f(cushion)} |',f'| Early monthly envelope | **{f(runrate)}** |','', 'The cushion is not a tax calculation or a promise it covers every invoice. Resend uses the two-account minimum illustration pending actual provider-approved critical/merchant stream configuration; usage can increase. Map/update/build limits, jobs, cloud traffic and storage have separate usage drivers. Staffing/review work is not funded simply by a cheap software minimum. Do not add these figures again on top of overlapping variable/fixed allocations in ECONOMICS-RESULTS; reconcile cost buckets.','', 'Media/file usage now has an explicit £10 monthly reserve. This raises the previous £217.55 estimate to £229.55, including the same 20% cushion. Reconcile actual Blob/storage/operations/transfer costs with included Vercel usage rather than charging twice. The reserve is a planning allowance, not a supplier package or guaranteed ceiling.','', '## Optional review/device-funded launch scenario','', '| Item | GBP |','| --- | ---: |']
for k,v in oneoff.items():lines.append(f'| {k.replace("_"," ")} | {f(v)} |')
lines += [f'| Total | **{f(upfront)}** |','', 'Apple/domain amounts include the stated first-year cash commitment, not another monthly charge in the run-rate table. Google registration is one-time. Legal/accounting/security/device/sample figures are reserves to obtain actual scope/quotes, not claimed supplier rates. Existing suitable devices or later quotes can change the need. No review purchased, no adviser retained and no certificates/store approvals obtained.','', '## Cash/runway examples','', '| Planning case | Estimated cash |','| --- | ---: |',f'| Upfront allowances + 3 months early platform envelope | {f(upfront+3*runrate)} |',f'| Upfront allowances + 6 months early platform envelope | {f(upfront+6*runrate)} |',f'| Same 6 months + illustrative £3,000/month engineering allowance | {f(upfront+6*(runrate+engineering))} |','', 'These exclude initial build/design/engineering cost, founder pay, acquisition, unquoted insurance/company/legal scope, significant usage growth, hardware stock/fulfilment and every unbudgeted item. Founder effort is work even if no immediate cash wage is paid. £3,000/month is an illustrative allowance, not a quote that fully staffs/builds this ecosystem. Do not pitch the £230-ish cloud/operations envelope as the cost of the whole company or as proof of profitability.','', '## Current package recommendation, unchanged','', '| Plan | Monthly proposed headline | What the business is buying | Marketing email sends/month |','| --- | ---: | --- | ---: |', '| Free | £0 | Good branded mini-space, 5 live offers, 30 new bookings/orders/month, basic supported work, eligible deposits, team access, customer return, native reviews/reporting and QR | 0 |','| Core | £12 | Everyday supported booking/classes/quotes/native commerce, stock/fulfilment, Google/Outlook calendar connection, richer appearance, custom-domain connection, public business/team Wallet cards and operational reports | 250 |','| Pro | £24 | Core plus supported merchant rewards/Wallet, repeat/series/package/quote/marketing recipes and deeper analytics | 1,000 |','| Business | £49 | Pro plus up to 3 managed locations, cross-location oversight, delegated/custom-role tools, advanced operational exports/automation and staffed priority queue | 3,000 |','', 'Proposed headline treatment includes applicable VAT in the current model, subject actual registration/supply review. No per-member fee. Essential operational email is included for accepted work. All rows mean genuinely supported workflows with enforced access/limits, not every regulated category or digital native purchase automatically permitted. PACKAGE-COMPARISON remains the detailed feature matrix; PRICING-DECISION is the commercial authority. No prices changed in this pass.','', '## Optional purchases and exclusions','', '| Item | Proposed treatment |','| --- | --- |','| UK SMS | Same service all plans: £9/100 units or £39/500; unit is provider-billed segment; auto top-up off |','| Card processing | Merchant pays actual provider fees; no proposed Taplo transaction commission |','| Domain | Connection included Core+; registration/renewal/transfer deliberately priced per actual registrar/TLD |','| NFC accessories | Separate product, shipping/replacement/returns and stable-link promise |','| Reward value | Merchant funds its actual discounts/free items/services; not subsidised by Taplo subscription |','| Business above 3 locations | No price or unsupported promise invented; separately assess scope before offering |','| WhatsApp / external-shop sync / public headless | Not standard launch inclusions; no silent extra bill |','| Custom work | No bespoke development entitlement hidden in the software price |','', 'A Core owner using no SMS can use the software for £12. Buying 100 units gives an initial £21 bill; 600 units gives £60 with the proposed packs. Long/Unicode content can consume more than one unit; do not conceal SMS-heavy total cost in a cheap base price. Existing paid units/allowance/cancellation treatment follows reviewed account/exit terms.','', '## What must be reconciled next','', 'Actual provider entities/regions/risk modes/quotes; complete launch category/native SKU scope; support/trust rota and workload budget; agreed recovery/security/legal evidence; meaningful merchant task and willingness-to-pay observations. Maintain stable pricing defaults while new material evidence is gathered rather than guessing a new price each conversation. Run contracts/calculate-launch-budget.py to reproduce this readout.']
(R.parent/'LAUNCH-BUDGET-AND-PACKAGE-READOUT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
print(json.dumps({k:out[k] for k in ['monthly_operating_envelope','upfront_total','three_month_runway_excluding_build_pay','six_month_runway_excluding_build_pay','six_month_runway_with_engineering_allowance']},indent=2))
